<title>JAPAN: Sakura Bank to name Okada as new president in June.</title>
<headline>Sakura Bank to name Okada as new president in June.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sakura Bank Ltd's executive director Akishige Okada will succeed Shunsaku Hashimoto as president of the bank on June 1, a source at the bank said on Friday.</p>
<p>Sakura, one of the top 10 commercial banks in Japan, will also appoint another executive director of the bank, Masahiro Takasaki, as the new chairman to suceed Kenichi Suematsu on June 1.</p>
<p>Hashimoto and Suematsu will remain in the board as advisors, the source said.</p>
</text>
